the administration is also dealing with  the public relations mess tonight  involving immigrant children officials  insist reports that nearly 1,500 kids  are lost art is not true chief national  correspondent ed Henry looks at the  facts tonight when Ivanka Trump posted  this photo with her young son this  weekend that Trump haters got triggered  unleashing online attacks charging she  does not care about migrant kids and  demanding to know where are the children  a reference to allegations that over  1400 migrant children have gone missing  and blamed President Trump for ordering  they be separated from their illegal  immigrant parents even the White House  spokesman Hogan Gidley  and officials at the Department of  Health and Human Services fired back  today none of those charges are true  that is an inaccurate characterization  of what happened this month Attorney  General Jeff Sessions traveled to Texas  to announce a new policy the government  will try to prosecute everyone who  crosses the southwest border illegally  even those seeking asylum that will lead  to some parents being separated from  their children which is already part of  existing law if you are smuggling a  child then we will prosecute you and  that child may be separated from you as  required by law the fourteen hundred and  seventy five kids who allegedly went  missing arrived at the border from  October to December 2017 months before  the sessions policy went into effect  secondly HHS officials point out those  kids were part of a total of seven  thousand six hundred and thirty five  children they surveyed over those three  months who showed up at the border  without parents so they were not  separated from them Trump administration  officials took the extra step of placing  the over 7,000 kids with adult sponsors  in the u.s. HHS found six thousand and  seventy five of the kids still living  with sponsors 52 living with someone  else  28 had run away five were deported  leaving 1475 unaccounted for HHS  officials say some of their sponsors are  here illegally and likely dodging the  government's attempts to contact them  eric Horgan the HHS official  in charge of the program stating quote  the assertion that unaccompanied alien  children are lost is completely false  this is a classic example of the adage  no good deed goes unpunished that did  not stop former Obama officials like Jon  Favreau and journalists like hadass  Gould of CNN from compounding the  mischaracterizations tweeting this photo  from a-z central.com a website  affiliated with USA Today of Latino  children being held in cages to claim it  shows President Trump's policies or mean  the problem that image was taken in 2014  when Barack Obama was president  Republican Marco Rubio's are frequent  critic of the president but he gave him  some political cover on this one pressed  on whether the law dealing with  separating parents from kids should be  fixed Rubio told CBS the better law to  change is actually securing the border  right and thank you
 

